[Term]
id: DOID:0050118
name: La Crosse encephalitis
def: "A viral infectious disease that results_in inflammation located_in brain, has_material_basis_in La Crosse virus (Orthobunyavirus lacrosseense), which is primarily transmitted_by treehole mosquito (Ochlerotatus triseriatus) but also Asian tiger mosquito (Aedes albopictus) and Asian bush mosquito (Aedes japonicus). The infection has_symptom seizures, has_symptom headache, has_symptom fever, has_symptom coma, and has_symptom paralysis. (DO)" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Crosse_encephalitis "DO", https://www.cdc.gov/la-crosse-encephalitis/about/ "DO", https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562248/ "DO"]
