[Term]
id: DOID:0050192
name: Nipah virus encephalitis
def: "A viral infectious disease that results_in inflammation located_in brain, has_material_basis_in Nipah virus (Henipavirus nipahense), which is transmitted_by direct contact with sick person or animals, or their contaminated tissues. The infection has_symptom dizziness, has_symptom drowsiness, has_symptom altered consciousness, has_symptom disorientation, and has_symptom coma. (DO)" [https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9345211/ "DO", https://www.cdc.gov/nipah-virus/about/ "DO", https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK570576/ "DO", https://www.who.int/csr/disease/nipah/en/ "DO", PMID:19141846 "DO"]
