[Term]
id: DOID:0050194
name: Argentine hemorrhagic fever
def: "A viral infectious disease that is a hemorrhagic fever, has_material_basis_in Junin virus (Mammarenavirus juninense), which is transmitted_by rodent, Calomys musculinus. The infection has_symptom fever, has_symptom fatigue, has_symptom malaise, has_symptom leukopenia, has_symptom thrombocytopenia, and has_symptom hemorrhagic manifestations. (DO)" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentine_hemorrhagic_fever "DO", http://www.jstor.org/stable/30129873?seq=1 "DO"]
xref: MONDO:0017874
