[Term]
id: DOID:0050246
name: granulomatous amebic encephalitis
def: "A parasitic protozoa infectious disease that results in infection of the brain caused by Acanthamoeba or Balamuthia mandrillaris. The symptoms include headaches, altered mental status, and focal neurologic deficit, which progresses over several weeks to death. (DO)" [http://www.dpd.cdc.gov/dpdx/HTML/FreeLivingAmebic.htm "DO"]
