[Term]
id: DOID:0050260
name: dioctophymiasis
def: "A parasitic helminthiasis infectious disease that involves parasitic infection by the nematode Dioctophyme renale in humans after eating undercooked food. The larvae are found in the subcutaneous nodules and kidneys. (DO)" [http://www.dpd.cdc.gov/dpdx/HTML/Dioctophymiasis.htm "DO"]
