[Term]
id: DOID:0060343
name: glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis
def: "An osteoporosis caused by chronic glucocorticoid use. Glucocorticoids impair the replication, differentiation and function of osteoblasts and induce the apoptosis of mature osteoblasts and osteocytes; the also favor osteoclastogenesis leading to an increase in bone resorption. (DO)" [PMID:17566815 "DO", PMID:22870429 "DO"]
