[Term]
id: DOID:0080990
name: King Denborough syndrome
alt_id: DOID:9003967
alt_id: MIM:619542
def: "A myopathy that is characterized by distinctive facies, ptosis, downslanted palpebral fissures, widely spaced eyes, epicanthal folds, low-set ears, malar hypoplasia, micrognathia, high-arched palate, clinodactyly, single palmar crease, pectus excavatum, winging of the scapulae, lumbar lordosis, and mild thoracic scoliosis. Pathogenic variants in RYR1 have been found in some individuals with King-Denborough syndrome. (DO)" [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK1146/ "DO"]
synonym: "Anesthetic-induced malignant hyperpyrexia in children" EXACT []
synonym: "King syndrome" EXACT []
