[Term]
id: DOID:12206
name: dengue hemorrhagic fever
def: "A dengue disease that occurs when a person experiences a second infection with a heterologous Dengue virus (Orthoflavivirus denguei) serotype, which is transmitted_by Aedes mosquito bite. The infection has_symptom hemorrhagic lesions of the skin, has_symptom thrombocytopenia, has_symptom reduction in the fluid part of the blood, and has_symptom high fever. Four distinct Dengue virus serotypes have been identified. (DO)" [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC88892/pdf/cm000480.pdf "DO", http://www.nlm.nih.gov/MEDLINEPLUS/ency/article/001373.htm "DO", https://www.merriam-webster.com/medical/dengue%20hemorrhagic%20fever "DO"]
