[Term]
id: DOID:12570
name: phacolytic glaucoma
def: "A phacogenic glaucoma that is characterized by acute onset of open-angle glaucoma secondary to a leaking mature or hypermature cataract and has_symptom chronic progressive vision loss with acute onset of pain, redness, and blurry vision. Phacolytic glaucomas are caused by direct obstruction of aqueous outflow pathways from leaking cataractous lens proteins. (DO)" [PMID:30950286 "DO"]
xref: ICD9CM:365.51
is_a: DOID:12571 ! phacogenic glaucoma
created_by: rgd
creation_date: 2017-10-25T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: DOID:12571
name: phacogenic glaucoma
def: "A glaucoma characterized by glaucomatous optic atrophy secondary to a lens abnormality and has_symptom progressive decreased vision, especially decreased peripheral vision. Phacogenic glaucoma can be caused by cataracts, trauma to the eye, or age-related damage that obstructs aqueous outflow, leading to inappropriately increased intraocular pressure and eventual optic nerve atrophy with associated vision loss. (DO)" [https://eyewiki.aao.org/Lens_Induced_Glaucomas "DO"]
