[Term]
id: DOID:12935
name: alcoholic cardiomyopathy
def: "Disease of CARDIAC MUSCLE resulting from chronic excessive alcohol consumption. Myocardial damage can be caused by: (1) a toxic effect of alcohol; (2) malnutrition in alcoholics such as THIAMINE DEFICIENCY; or (3) toxic effect of additives in alcoholic beverages such as COBALT. This disease is usually manifested by DYSPNEA and palpitations with CARDIOMEGALY and congestive heart failure (HEART FAILURE)." [MESH:D002310]
synonym: "alcohol-induced heart muscle disease" EXACT []
synonym: "dilated cardiomyopathy secondary to alcohol" EXACT []
