[Term]
id: DOID:3481
name: septicemic plague
def: "A plague that results_in infection located_in vasculature where bacterial endotoxins cause coagulation, which leads to formation of tiny clots throughout the body. The infection has_symptom fever, has_symptom chills, has_symptom prostration, has_symptom abdominal pain, has_symptom shock and has_symptom bleeding into skin and other organs. (DO)" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_%28disease%29#Septicemic_plague "DO", http://www.cdc.gov/ncidod/dvbid/plague/facts.htm "DO"]
