[Term]
id: DOID:4479
name: pseudohypoaldosteronism
def: "A heterogeneous group of disorders characterized by renal electrolyte transport dysfunctions. Congenital forms are rare autosomal disorders characterized by neonatal hypertension, HYPERKALEMIA, increased RENIN activity and ALDOSTERONE concentration. The Type I features HYPERKALEMIA with sodium wasting; Type II, HYPERKALEMIA without sodium wasting. Pseudohypoaldosteronism can be the result of a defective renal electrolyte transport protein or acquired after KIDNEY TRANSPLANTATION." [MESH:D011546]
synonym: "familial hyperpotassemia and hypertension" EXACT []
synonym: "Familial Hypertensive Hyperkalemia" EXACT []
synonym: "Familial Hypertensive Hyperkalemias" EXACT []
