[Term]
id: DOID:4866
name: salivary gland adenoid cystic carcinoma
def: "A salivary gland carcinoma that is characterized by a distinctive pattern in which abnormal nests or cords of epithelial cells surround and/or infiltrate ducts or glandular structures within the affected organ. These structures are typically filled with a mucous-like material or contain abnormal fibrous membranes. (DO)" [https://oralcancerfoundation.org/facts/rare/adenoid-cystic-carcinoma/ "DO"]
synonym: "adenoid cystic cancer" EXACT []
xref: NCI:C2970
xref: NCI:C8026
