id: DOID:9000408
name: Porokeratosis 3, Multiple Types
def: "Porokeratosis is a rare skin disorder characterized by one or more annular plaques with a surrounding raised horny border that spreads centrifugally. Variants of porokeratosis have been described that differ in morphologic shapes, distribution, and clinical course. However, several families with expression of more than one variant of porokeratosis among members, and individuals expressing more than one variant, have been reported, suggesting that the distinctions among these variants may be artificial. Multiple types of porokeratosis (POROK3) are caused by heterozygous mutation in the MVK gene on chromosome 12q24. (OMIM)" []
