[Term]
id: DOID:9001127
name: Porokeratosis 2, Palmar, Plantar, and Disseminated Type
alt_id: MIM:175850
def: "Porokeratosis is a rare skin disorder characterized by one or more annular plaques with a surrounding raised horny border that spreads centrifugally. Variants of porokeratosis have been described that differ in morphologic shapes, distribution, and clinical course. However, families with expression of more than one variant of porokeratosis among members, and individuals expressing more than one variant, have been reported, suggesting that the distinctions among these variants may be artificial. Porokeratosis palmaris plantaris et disseminata (PPPD) is a subtype in which lesions initially develop on the palms and soles, but later involve other parts of the body, including the trunk and limbs. POROK2 maps to chromosome 12q24. (OMIM)" []
synonym: "POROK2" EXACT []
synonym: "porokeratosis palmaris et plantaris disseminata" EXACT []
synonym: "porokeratosis, palmar, plantar, and disseminated" EXACT []
