def: "This disease is defined as the lack of foveal depression with continuity of all neurosensory retinal layers in the presumed foveal area. Foveal hypoplasia as an isolated entity is a rare phenomenon; it is usually described in association with other ocular disorders, such as aniridia, microphthalmia, albinism, or achromatopsia. All reported cases of foveal hypoplasia have been accompanied by decreased visual acuity and nystagmus." [MIM:136520]
