[Term]
id: DOID:9003994
name: PERIPHERAL MOTOR NEUROPATHY, CHILDHOOD-ONSET, BIOTIN-RESPONSIVE
def: "This disease is an autosomal recessive disorder characterized predominantly by the onset of distal muscle weakness and atrophy late in the first decade of life. The disorder predominantly affects the upper limbs and hands, resulting in difficulties with fine motor skills. Electrophysiologic studies and muscle biopsy are consistent with chronic denervation with axonal and demyelinating features. Sensation is intact, and patients have normal cognitive development. Treatment with biotin, pantothenic acid, and lipoic acid may result in clinical improvement." [MIM:619903]
synonym: "COMNB" EXACT []
