[Term]
id: DOID:9004843
name: Familial Horizontal Gaze Palsy with Progressive Scoliosis, 1
def: "HGPPS is an autosomal recessive neurologic disorder characterized by eye movement abnormalities apparent from birth and childhood-onset progressive scoliosis. These features are associated with a developmental malformation of the brainstem including hypoplasia of the pons and cerebellar peduncles and defective decussation of certain neuronal systems. Cognitive function is normal. Familial horizontal gaze palsy with progressive scoliosis-1 (HGPPS1) is caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the ROBO3 gene on chromosome 11q24. (OMIM)" []
