[Term]
id: DOID:9007235
name: Hydatidiform Mole, Recurrent, 4
def: "Hydatidiform mole is a human pregnancy with abnormal or no embryonic development and excessive trophoblastic proliferation. Partial hydatidiform moles have a triploid dispermic genome, with 2 sets of paternal chromosomes and 1 set of maternal chromosomes; complete hydatidiform moles have a diploid androgenetic genome with all chromosomes originating from 1 (monospermic) or 2 (dispermic) sperms, and no maternal chromosomes. Recurrent hydatidiform mole-4 (HYDM4) is caused by homozygous mutation in the C11ORF80 gene on chromosome 11q13. (OMIM)" []
synonym: "HYDM4" EXACT []
synonym: "TOP6BL-RELATED CONDITION" EXACT []
