name: NEURODEGENERATION, CHILDHOOD-ONSET, WITH MULTISYSTEM INVOLVEMENT DUE TO MITOCHONDRIAL DYSFUNCTION
def: "This disease is an autosomal recessive syndromic disorder characterized primarily by neurologic deficits. Patients show global developmental delay and variably impaired intellectual development with speech delay apparent from infancy. Affected individuals have hypotonia, poor feeding, poor overall growth, and respiratory distress early in life. The disorder is progressive and has features suggestive of a mitochondrial disorder: cataracts, cardiomyopathy, diabetes mellitus, combined oxidative phosphorylation deficiency, and increased lactate." [MIM:620089]
