[Term]
id: DOID:9008147
name: Cancer, Alopecia, Pigment Dyscrasia, Onychodystrophy, and Keratoderma
def: "CAPOK syndrome is characterized by onset of symptoms in the first year of life, with the development of progressive alopecia, hypo- and hyperpigmented macular skin lesions, palmoplantar keratoderma, and nail dystrophy. Beginning in the third decade of life, patients develop recurrent squamous cell carcinomas. Some patients may have brittle teeth resulting in tooth loss, and multinodular goiter has been observed. CAPOK can be caused by homozygous mutation in the SASH1 gene on chromosome 6q24. (OMIM)" []
synonym: "CAPOK" EXACT []
