[Term]
id: DOID:9009315
name: Idiopathic Generalized Epilepsy
alt_id: DOID:1827
def: "This s a type of epilepsy where seizures originate from both sides of the brain simultaneously, with no identifiable structural abnormality. It is characterized by generalized seizures, including absence, myoclonic, and generalized tonic-clonic seizures. IGE is often considered genetic, with a predisposition to seizures due to genetic factors." [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK546611/]
synonym: "EIG" EXACT []
synonym: "EIG1" NARROW []
synonym: "EPILEPSY, JUVENILE MYOCLONIC, SUSCEPTIBILITY TO, 10" RELATED []
synonym: "genetic generalized epilepsy" EXACT []
synonym: "idiopathic generalized epilepsy, susceptibility to, 1" RELATED []
synonym: "IGE EPILEPSY, IDIOPATHIC GENERALIZED, SUSCEPTIBILITY TO, 1" RELATED []
synonym: "primary generalized epilepsy" EXACT []
xref: MESH:C562694
xref: MIM:600669
xref: MONDO:0005579
is_a: DOID:1827 ! generalized epilepsy
created_by: mtutaj
creation_date: 2025-03-04T16:30:19Z

