[Term]
id: DOID:9009322
name: NEURODEVELOPMENTAL DISORDER WITH PROGRESSIVE SPASTICITY AND BRAIN ABNORMALITIES
def: "This disease is an autosomal recessive disorder apparent in infancy or early childhood and characterized by global developmental delay with moderate to severely impaired intellectual development, poor or absent speech, hypotonia, and delayed walking or inability to walk. Additional features include microcephaly, various types of seizures, nonspecific dysmorphic facial features, ocular anomalies (strabismus, nystagmus, gaze palsy), and cerebellar signs, such as ataxic gait or tremor. Brain imaging shows cerebral and/or cerebellar hypoplasia and delayed myelination." [MIM:621102]
synonym: "NEDPSB" EXACT []
xref: MIM:621102
is_a: DOID:9004429 ! Neurodevelopmental Disorders
