[Term]
id: DOID:9009333
name: NEURODEGENERATION, EARLY-CHILDHOOD-ONSET, WITH RETINITIS PIGMENTOSA, SENSORINEURAL HEARING LOSS, AND DEMYELINATING PERIPHERAL NEUROPATHY
def: "This disease is an autosomal recessive complex neurodegenerative disorder with onset in early childhood (around 3 years of age) after normal initial development. Affected individuals have progressive walking difficulties (spasticity or ataxia) resulting in loss of ambulation, progressive visual impairment and blindness due to retinitis pigmentosa, sensorineural hearing loss, demyelinating peripheral neuropathy, and severely impaired intellectual development with poor or absent speech." [MIM:621129]
