id: DOID:9009335
name: Cranioectodermal dysplasia 5
def: "A rare autosomal recessive ciliopathy characterized by dysmorphic features including sagittal craniosynostosis, dolichocephaly, frontal bossing, growth retardation, rhizomelic shortening of the upper and lower limbs, narrow thorax, and protuberant abdomen. Caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the IFT140 gene on chromosome 16p13." [MIM:621180]
