[Term]
id: DOID:9009365
name: ICHAD syndrome
def: "A syndrome characterized by Immunodysregulation, Craniofacial anomalies, Hearing impairment, Athelia, and Developmental delay with the onset of these features soon after birth or in early infancy. Affected individuals have recurrent infections, mainly respiratory. The immunologic disorder belongs to a subtype of inborn errors of immunity called 'primary immune regulatory disorders' (PIRDs). Additional features include poor feeding, global developmental delay, and dysmorphic facial features with cleft palate." [MIM:621234]
