[Term]
id: DOID:9009410
name: cystic fibrosis-related diabetes
def: "This disease is a distinct form of diabetes common in cystic fibrosis (CF), caused by thick mucus scarring the pancreas, leading to insulin insufficiency and resistance. Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes shares traits with Type 1 (insulin deficiency) and Type 2 (insulin resistance) but stems from CF's direct impact on pancreatic function, requiring careful monitoring and management." [https://www.cff.org/managing-cf/cystic-fibrosis-related-diabeteshttps\://www.cff.org/managing-cf/cystic-fibrosis-related-diabetes]
synonym: "CFRD" EXACT []
