[Term]
id: DOID:9009435
name: non-CF bronchiectasis
def: "A bronchial disease not caused by cystic fibrosis that is a chronic inflammatory condition of one or more bronchi or bronchioles marked by dilatation and loss of elasticity of the walls resulting from damage to the airway wall leading to the formation of small sacs on the bronchial wall and impairment of cilia mobility in the lung. Inflammation of the bronchial wall increases mucus secretion which serves as a breeding ground for bacteria. Non-CF bronchiectasis is caused by repeated respiratory infections, immune deficiency disorders, hereditary disorders (primary ciliary dyskinesia), mechanical factors (inhaled object or a lung tumor) or inhaling toxic substances." [DOID:9563]
synonym: "non-cystic fibrosis bronchiectasis" EXACT []
is_a: DOID:9563 ! bronchiectasis
created_by: caripark
creation_date: 2026-03-23T13:36:24Z

