[Term]
id: DOID:9392
name: tracheitis
def: "A tracheal disease which involves bacterial infection of the trachea often caused by Staphylococcus aureus and streptococci that follows a recent viral upper respiratory infection. The symptoms include barking croup cough, loud squeaking noise while breathing, scratchy feeling in the throat, high fever, and production of large amounts of pus-filled secretions. (DO)" [http://www.merck.com/mmpe/sec19/ch277/ch277j.html?qt=tracheitis&alt=sh "DO"]
